      "The source creator analysed the three most popular videos from the reference channel rather than relying on a single example. For each video, the research document recorded:\n1. Video title.\n2. View count.\n3. Scene duration.\n4. Visual description.\n5. Script or narration.\n6. A screenshot representing the scene.\nThis is a simple but powerful way to move from vague inspiration to a production blueprint.\nResearch workflow\nStep 1: Select a small sample.\nChoose three strong examples from one channel or format. Prioritise videos that clearly demonstrate the pattern you want to understand.",
      "Step 2: Watch each video more than once.\nFirst watch for the overall premise and emotional effect. On the second pass, pause at every meaningful change in action, framing, or information.",
