      "Step 5: Separate the general pattern from the creator's specifics.\nThe general pattern may be useful; the exact subject, wording, character, visual identity, and scene choices should remain original.\nScene-analysis template\nField\tWhat to record\nVideo title\tExact title of the reference video\nViews at time of research\tThe displayed view count and date checked\nScene number\tSequential number\nApproximate duration\tHow long the scene remains on screen\nVisual action\tWhat the viewer actually sees\nNarration / text\tSpoken line or on-screen wording\nViewer question\tWhat the scene makes the viewer wonder\nTransition\tHow the next scene follows\nFunction\tHook, assessment, action, progress, build, or payoff\nScreenshot\tA still that helps explain the composition",
