      "A strong reveal:\n- Shows the final result for long enough to register.\n- Reuses the original angle or image when possible.\n- Makes the before/after difference obvious.\n- Feels like the answer to the opening declaration.\n- Does not introduce a new, unrelated idea at the last second.\nThe complete narrative at a glance\nPhase\tViewer experience\tProduction question\nDeclare\t“What is going to happen?”\tWhat promise creates an open loop?\nAssessment\t“How difficult is the starting point?”\tWhat evidence establishes the challenge?\nIsolate\t“How is the task being tackled?”\tWhich small actions are visually satisfying?\nProcess\t“What work is happening behind the scenes?”\tWhat can be compressed into a montage?\nBuild\t“Is the result coming together?”\tWhat visible steps signal progress?\nReveal\t“Did they actually do it?”\tWhat final comparison closes the loop?",
