      "Problem\tLikely issue\tPractical response\nThe idea feels like a copy\tOnly the subject or surface details have changed\tReturn to the underlying storytelling mechanics and develop a distinct premise\nThe opening feels weak\tThe declaration is vague or the starting condition is unclear\tState the outcome and show the subject immediately\nThe video feels repetitive\tSeveral scenes perform the same narrative function\tGive each phase a distinct job and remove redundant shots\nAI images look inconsistent\tReferences or descriptions are not stable\tReuse environment and subject references; specify continuity requirements\nAnimation looks unnatural\tThe prompt asks for too many movements or the still is weak\tSimplify the action and regenerate the still before animating\nThe first scene is technically acceptable but boring\tIt lacks a clear focal point or visual question\tRework the composition; the Polaroid “before” idea is one example from the case study\nNarration feels disconnected\tScript was written without checking the actual generated clips\tEdit the script and timeline together\nThe edit feels slow\tDead air or repetitive process shots remain\tTighten pauses and compress repeated actions\nThe reveal is disappointing\tThe final state is not clearly different from the starting state\tShow a direct comparison and hold the final result long enough\nViews slow down\tDistribution has temporarily reduced\tRecord the data, review retention and feedback, and avoid declaring the video dead too early\nOne upload performs well but the next does not\tOne result has been mistaken for a repeatable formula\tTreat each upload as a new test; preserve the core promise while varying the story\nMonetisation is uncertain\tThe creator assumes AI use alone determines eligibility\tReview current YouTube policies and ensure the channel is original, varied, rights-compliant, and accurately disclosed"
