      "The long-term value of the experiment is not the headline view count. It is the operating loop:",
      "Research → Extract the format → Choose an original concept → Script → Generate → Review → Edit → Publish → Measure → Improve.",
      "Use the following cycle for each upload.\nBefore production\n- [ ] Study a small set of relevant high-performing examples.\n- [ ] Identify the narrative mechanics rather than copying the surface.\n- [ ] Validate the concept against relatability, emotional hook, and completion compulsion.\n- [ ] Confirm that the idea is original and visually feasible.\n- [ ] Write the six-phase outline.\nDuring production\n- [ ] Establish environment and subject references.\n- [ ] Generate one scene at a time.\n- [ ] Check visual consistency.\n- [ ] Iterate on the opening and other high-impact scenes.\n- [ ] Draft and refine narration.\n- [ ] Assemble the edit and remove dead air.\n- [ ] Add rights-cleared music and readable captions.\nBefore publishing\n- [ ] Confirm the title accurately describes the video.\n- [ ] Write a relevant description.\n- [ ] Use accurate audience settings.\n- [ ] Check any required synthetic-content disclosures.\n- [ ] Confirm rights to visual, audio, and voice assets.\n- [ ] Watch the final export in full.\nAfter publishing\n- [ ] Record views and retention metrics at consistent checkpoints.\n- [ ] Note distribution changes without assuming their cause.\n- [ ] Review comments and audience feedback.\n- [ ] Identify the strongest and weakest moments.\n- [ ] Prepare a distinct follow-up idea.\n- [ ] Update the production process based on evidence, not one emotional reaction to the view graph."
